  "body": "## What changed\n\n`ToolBody` now stores an ordered `pieces: Vec<BodyPiece>` table while keeping `facets` and `frame` as the merged body. Each piece records its label, facet count, rigid placement, and transformed STEP coordinate systems (`BodyCsys`).\n\n`tool_body_assembly` and `tool_body_mate` load piece files, mate child `MCS` frames onto parent `CSW*` frames (or explicit named parent and child frames), enforce the facet budget, and rebuild merged facets cleanly. Ambiguous, missing, mismatched, or single-piece-removal inputs fail with named error messages.\n\n`SetToolBody::attach_piece`, `SetToolBody::attach_loaded_piece`, and `SetToolBody::remove_piece` update modular assemblies in one undoable command step. `ToolBodyDto` serializes `pieces` additively and omits the key for single-piece bodies without CSYS metadata.\n\nMCP tools `attach_tool_body_piece` and `remove_tool_body_piece`, `get_tool_body` (`pieces`), and the Tool Editor Modular Assembly section expose piece attachment and removal to agents and users.\n\n## Cause\n\nSingle-piece tool body replacement discarded prior pieces when a user attached a clamping unit, extension, or modular lathe head from vendor STEP/STL/OBJ files. No CSYS mating or piece tracking existed to align multi-piece assemblies or judge them together in simulation.\n\n## Tests\n\nPinning tests written before the fix (verified red before implementation, green after):\n- `crates/app/tests/tool_body_assembly.rs`: `lathe_head_and_clamping_unit_mate_by_iso13399_csys_and_judge_together`, `three_piece_spindle_assembly_persists_in_camproj_and_camtools_and_draws_all_pieces`, `modular_assembly_refuses_ambiguous_missing_and_over_budget_pieces_by_name`, `mcp_attach_and_remove_tool_body_piece_roundtrips_and_undoes`.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/tool_body_assembly.rs`: `editor_attaches_and_removes_modular_lathe_pieces_in_one_undo_step`, `editor_mates_spindle_pieces_with_explicit_csys_and_refuses_bad_names`.\n\nMutation checks (reverted guard failed red, restored guard passed green):\n- Skipped serializing `pieces` in `project/tool_body_wire.rs`: `three_piece_spindle_assembly_persists_in_camproj_and_camtools_and_draws_all_pieces` failed (piece count 1 != 3); passed after restore.\n- Bypassed ambiguous CSYS refusal in `tool_body_mate.rs`: `modular_assembly_refuses_ambiguous_missing_and_over_budget_pieces_by_name` failed; passed after restore.\n- Disabled single-piece removal guard in `tool_body_assembly.rs`: `modular_assembly_refuses_ambiguous_missing_and_over_budget_pieces_by_name` failed; passed after restore.\n\nGates and checks (green):\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test tool_body_assembly --test vendor_tool_body --test mcp_tool_body --test tool_body --test tool_csys` (35 passed, 0 failed).\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib tool_body_assembly` (2 passed, 0 failed).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` (0 warnings).\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` (all app and ui suites passed, 0 failed).\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. `git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nVendor files with multiple non-unique `MCS`/`CSW` frames beyond the synthetic STEP test fixtures were not manually loaded in a live GUI window; all mating, persistence, simulation, and UI undo paths run headless under `tool_body_assembly` and `camcraft-ui` tests.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nThe following open PRs touch the same file in different functions (whichever merges second refreshes):\n- `.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`: #1722, #1718, #1695\n- `crates/app/src/lib.rs`: #1699, #1681, #1209\n- `crates/app/src/schema.rs`: #1699\n- `crates/ui/src/state.rs`: #1711, #1699, #1330\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/mod.rs`: #1710, #1330, #1209\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests.rs`: #1685, #1330, #1209\n\nProcess change: yes\nChangelog: Support modular multi-piece tool body assembly from vendor STEP/STL/OBJ models (#361, #1040).\nFixes #361\n\n\n## UI screenshots\n\nBefore: the parent editor Body page, with one imported ISO 13399 head and no assembly controls.\n\n![Tool editor before assembly controls](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/issue/361-modular-tool-assembly/docs/review/1744/before.png)\n\nAfter: the editor with the head and clamping unit assembled, the piece list, and the target-piece selector set to piece 1.\n\n![Tool editor with assembled tool and target-piece control](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/issue/361-modular-tool-assembly/docs/review/1744/after.png)\n\nThese are actual egui editor renders from the headless UI harness at 1560×1100. The before capture uses the parent commit's unchanged `tool_body_page.rs`; the after capture uses this PR's editor. The synthetic STEP files are `tool_csys_box_iso13399.step` and `modular_clamp_unit.step`. Release snapshot PNGs are unchanged.\n",
